                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is tiring. You have to do something every single moment, otherwise you die. \nI also don't like the UI and the controls are clunky too often.\n\nBut there are 2 major problems that go hand in hand:\n\n1. big problem:\nPERMADEATH\n\nI have rarely seen a gameplay mechanic as worse as this one. If you die you start at 0 again, there is no meta-progression between runs.\nIt is single-handedly the reason why this game sucks. In many games, permadeath is not problematic at all, but here? \n\nSee: This game demands experimentation and learning, but you die VERY easily and VERY often, losing everything. It actively disincentivizes you. \nSo logically speaking, you should play it safe. But obviously that won't get you anywhere.\n\nI hope you see the issue. It's just stupid.\nPart of me is also convinced that this forced permadeath, among other things, is also just there to stretch playtime, like genuinely.\n\nPeep this: by adding a normal mode, you would legitimately cut this games playtime by a huuuge amount. It's actually crazy.\n\n2. big problem:\nGameplay-loop  / ressource gathering\n\nAt least 90% of your time and runs is spent ressource gathering + running around and waiting at night doing barely anything. It is abhorrent. It gets repetitive very quickly. The gameplay-loop simply sucks.\nWith not even 4 hours, it is apparent as can be and more importantly: boring. as. hell. \n\nIt's always: gather, gather, gather. Then eventually: you die.\nGathering time again for 20-40 minutes. Then you die. \nGathering. You die. \n\nAdditionally to that, you make babysteps every run BECAUSE you are so busy with the mundane stuff. In all of my runs, I have barely made any progress. I wanted to plant some crops at first but where do i get manure? From some animal? From myself? 6 runs and I still don't fucking know.\n\nNow you could look at the wiki to progress faster and give you a helping hand, sure. But then again, if a game has you looking at the fucking wiki in the first few fucking hours for the fucking basics, then the game is doing something very, veeery wrong. And also: congrats, you are basically admitting that the learning process is too slow, too vague and time-consuming. Which also speaks badly of the game.\n\nIt's a shame because DS really has neat art and style, the vibe is great and it seems genuinely complex. Almost every other aspect of this game is decent. \n\nHowever, the amount of time you have to invest to progress even a tiny bit is just way too much. This game also isn't difficult, as many claim it to be. It just punishes you with an absurd amount of lost time.  It's a time tax or artificial difficulty at best, or whatever you wanna call it.\n\n\nDon't Starve just simply does not respect your time. Not one bit. \n\n(Also: selling separate versions, one without multiplayer and one with, is insanely scummy bevahiour)",
